  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nCurrently all browsers stop form navigations if `window.stop()` is called synchronously after a form is submitted, e.g.:\n```html\n<form id=form action=\"foo\"></form>\n<script> form.submit(); stop(); </script>\n```\nhowever this is not part of the spec. Probably there should be some language in [abort-a-document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#abort-a-document-and-its-descendants) about [planned form navigations](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#planned-navigation).\n\n(Also the WPT [form-submit-and-window-stop.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/form-submit-and-window-stop.html?label=master&label=experimental&aligned&q=form-submit-and-window-stop.html) expects this behaviour.)\n",
